speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, on a point of order, while there is a natural interruption here between speakers, I think you will find consent for the following motion:
That notwithstanding any standing orders and usual practices of this House, all recorded divisions requested on Wednesday, December 3,1991 be deemed deferred until Monday, December 9, 1991 at 6 p.m.;
Second, that in relation to its consideration of credit and charge cards under Standing Order 108(2), eight members, one researcher and the Clerk of the Standing Committee on Consumer and Corporate Affairs be authorized to travel to Washington, D.C. February 4 and 5, 1992;
Third, that the subcommittee on arms exports of the Standing Committee on External Affairs and International Hade be authorized to travel to Winnipeg and Victoria from Monday, February 10, to Friday, February 14, 1992; and to Montreal and Halifax from Monday, February 24 to Friday 28, 1992, in order to hold hearings and visit companies and bases in relation to the subcommittee study on arms production and export; and
That the necessary staff accompany the subcommittee.
